        "Callas",
        "Sinthe",
        "Callas the Unfaithful"
      ],
      "keysecondary": [
        "Melus",
        "Navia",
        "Spina di Rosula"
      ],
      "comment": "Melus: Callas and the Sinthe case",
      "content": "Callas, the previous Spina di Rosula boss, was convicted of shooting his informant Jacques and died in a duel with Clorinde. Melus believes he was framed and says Sinthe, a popular drink made with Primordial Sea water, led to the dispute. Callas refused to yield in the duel and asked Clorinde to keep Navia safe.\n\nMelus says Callas was diagnosed with an illness leaving him less than five years, and chose to die in the arena rather than let his daughter see him weak. What Callas wanted to hand to Navia was \"not a parasol, but a sword\".",
